@startuml

start

:TCMS executes on preemptive RTOS;
:Manage via deterministic, priority-scheduled tasks;
fork
  :Traction;
fork again
  :Braking;
fork again
  :Doors;
fork again
  :Diagnostics;
end fork

:Station entry;
:Execute sequential state validation routine;
:Confirm zero speed via wheel speed sensor ISR;
:Check passenger doors are closed;
:Initiate safety interlock chain;
fork
  :Validate platform screen doors are closed;
fork again
  :Validate emergency brake actuator is released;
end fork
:Perform CRC-checked status query of traction FADEC;

  if (Validation successful?) then (yes)
    :Authorize train initialization;
    :Spawn concurrent, mutex-protected operations;

    fork
      :High-priority task manages door lock signaling;
    fork again
      :Lower-priority control loop;
      :Use ring buffer for sensor data;
      :Modulate traction force;
      :Monitor PMIC/BMS output；
      :Maintain current and rail voltage within safe operating limits;
    fork again
      :Watchdog-supervised state machine processes platform door closing signal;
      :Place traction system into standby;
    fork again
      :Separate monitoring task employs exponential backoff for CAN bus queries;
      :Poll platform door status;
      :Ensure complete closure before startup finalizes;
    end fork

  else (no)
  end if

:Transition to normal operational state;
:Archive all critical telemetry to non-volatile memory and fail-safe paths;
:Ensure graceful degradation in compliance with EN 50128/EN 50129;

stop

@enduml
